Subject: [PATCH 2/4] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's patch 2, built on
 ea41e6fc9): A GATE THAT READS THE PAST IS REFUSED ON A SHALLOW CLONE (the
 seat's planted case PV22). On a clone fifty commits deep lead-debt dated
 every arc by the history that was there and passed; on the same clone
 seal-order-unshown accused an arc whose first commit lay beyond the cut. A
 cut history gives a wrong answer either way. checkout_state now reads a
 shallow clone as shallow, at any depth, and the twelve gates of READS_HISTORY
 are refused on one in plain words, with what to run; the seven that ask only
 which files are tracked have all they need and are not refused. A clone made
 with a depth that reaches the first commit cuts nothing and is a full clone.
 The lock: two tests added to
 tests/test_gates_are_a_function_of_the_commit.py, both failing on the commit
 before (a shallow clone read as full; lead-debt answering ok). 0 of 19.

